prologue_5f0086bb		Let their spirits pass without suffering. Let their memories remain unspoiled.	game/02_prologue.rpy	249	"[what]"
prologue_e123e360		Let Your cloak be warm. Let their burdens fall at Your feet, Almighty Enoch.	game/02_prologue.rpy	250	"[what]"
prologue_b793fbc9		A young woman with silver hair knelt in the dust and shadow, her fingers cold against the bloodspattered floor.	game/02_prologue.rpy	252	"[what]"
prologue_2ca00c12		The torchlight flickered against her trembling form. She closed her eyes and spoke softly, her voice barely more than a breath.	game/02_prologue.rpy	253	"[what]"
prologue_be96aba6	kristin	Grant me strength to carry out your will: to lay these bodies to rest with reverence, to honor their passage, and to usher them into your sacred silence.	game/02_prologue.rpy	258	kristin "[what]"
prologue_ea1f796c		Two aldorith soldiers stood at the threshold, their faces sharp with impatience, their breath fogging faintly in the chill of the underground.	game/02_prologue.rpy	261	"[what]"
prologue_bda836c4	boy_ald	She's still praying. It's been five minutes.	game/02_prologue.rpy	269	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_17719736	girl_ald	You're right. We cannot linger. The rot will draw attention.	game/02_prologue.rpy	271	girl_ald "[what]"
prologue_e547938e		Kristin's voice quivered as she continued to whisper her prayer—begging Enoch to take their souls gently.	game/02_prologue.rpy	273	"[what]"
prologue_db005679		To let them find peace. To weigh the sins of the living, not the dead.	game/02_prologue.rpy	274	"[what]"
prologue_1987765e	boy_ald	Enough of this, Kristin.	game/02_prologue.rpy	277	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_8366c080		Kristin flinched as if struck. She turned, eyes wide, lips pale.	game/02_prologue.rpy	281	"[what]"
prologue_e73a95a6	kristin	I was only… I was praying to Lord Enoch.	game/02_prologue.rpy	286	kristin "[what]"
prologue_473d2a3a	girl_ald	A prayer that's lasted too long. For minutes, sister. We've listened. Are you certain you're not harboring doubts?	game/02_prologue.rpy	290	girl_ald "[what]"
prologue_be58ae3b	kristin	D-Doubts? No, sister.	game/02_prologue.rpy	293	kristin "[what]"
prologue_006431ae	kristin	But… What we did—what happened—was it really right? We killed the queen and her two sons.	game/02_prologue.rpy	295	kristin "[what]"
prologue_0505b239	boy_ald	What are you saying? That our Father was wrong?	game/02_prologue.rpy	299	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_4345d0fc	kristin	N-no! I would never—why would I?	game/02_prologue.rpy	301	kristin "[what]"
prologue_0202e072	girl_ald	Your blood-brother Svante didn't hesitate. He slit their throats without blinking. He was useful. You? You pray for corpses.	game/02_prologue.rpy	306	girl_ald "[what]"
prologue_dd21ca86	boy_ald	Useless.	game/02_prologue.rpy	308	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_a27932f6		Kristin dropped her gaze. Her hands trembled at her sides.	game/02_prologue.rpy	310	"[what]"
prologue_2253043c	kristin	I'm very sorry… I just—	game/02_prologue.rpy	315	kristin "[what]"
prologue_f3895085	boy_ald	We don't need you anymore. You're only stalling.	game/02_prologue.rpy	317	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_abcdc83e	boy_ald	Count Vasily might have better use for someone like you.	game/02_prologue.rpy	319	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_8b8116dc		She didn't argue. With her head bowed and hands trembling at her sides, Kristin turned and walked away.	game/02_prologue.rpy	322	"[what]"
prologue_dcee18e9		Her footsteps echoed faintly down the underground tunnel—slow and hesitant.	game/02_prologue.rpy	323	"[what]"
prologue_c030945b		The two Aldoriths watched her disappear into the dark before exchanging a glance.	game/02_prologue.rpy	327	"[what]"
prologue_61d22ff6		Their gazes drifted to the lifeless forms behind them: the Queen of Tianho, regal even in death, and her two sons, wrapped in the stillness of final silence.	game/02_prologue.rpy	328	"[what]"
prologue_56d92eaf	boy_ald	That Kristin… soft-hearted as ever.	game/02_prologue.rpy	330	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_38c4f93b	girl_ald	She won't last. We both know Father only kept her around to control Svante.	game/02_prologue.rpy	332	girl_ald "[what]"
prologue_948e1aac		They moved wordlessly to the bodies, the ritual of burial unfolding with grim familiarity.	game/02_prologue.rpy	334	"[what]"
prologue_a25cfc3e		Cloth unrolled. Blood wiped. Limbs bound with reverent efficiency.	game/02_prologue.rpy	335	"[what]"
prologue_6aa718a0		Their hands worked swiftly—mechanical, practiced—but there was a flicker of hesitation behind their eyes.	game/02_prologue.rpy	336	"[what]"
prologue_c4aa4407	boy_ald	Why do you think Father really wanted them dead?	game/02_prologue.rpy	339	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_620278a4	girl_ald	I don't know. And I really don't plan to ask. Best not to chase answers when you're already neck-deep in secrets.	game/02_prologue.rpy	340	girl_ald "[what]"
prologue_22f858fc		She reached for the Queen's hand, cold and graceful, and began to wrap the burial cloth tight around her wrist.	game/02_prologue.rpy	342	"[what]"
prologue_39d7b7a8	boy_ald	This feels… different. We've carried out assassinations before, but never like this.	game/02_prologue.rpy	345	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_5daf9cfc	boy_ald	A queen. Two princes. Royals of Tianho.	game/02_prologue.rpy	347	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_75d5506f	girl_ald	Exactly why we need to hurry. If anyone finds out what's buried down here—before the earth swallows it whole—we're finished.	game/02_prologue.rpy	349	girl_ald "[what]"
prologue_a0d094fd	boy_ald	Still… Svante didn't even blink. Just walked in and—	game/02_prologue.rpy	353	boy_ald "[what]"
prologue_ee9bf1a0	girl_ald	Cold as stone. That's why he's Father's favorite. A metal channeler with no hesitation? That's worth more than loyalty.	game/02_prologue.rpy	355	girl_ald "[what]"
prologue_fa01b36b	girl_ald	Which is why he still keeps that skank Kristin…	game/02_prologue.rpy	357	girl_ald "[what]"
