ch4_chunghee_qtc_8db8f86c		Aunt Ji-hye's face lit up with gratitude.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	642	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_e1269d85	ji_hye	Thank you, Chung.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	644	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_f737aff6		I clutched the amulet tighter in my hands, its glow pulsing softly like a heartbeat. Its light bathed us both in green.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	646	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_29ec32b8		Her mind was an open book to me—pages unfolding like petals of a flower, revealing memories that had been locked away in the recesses of her heart.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	647	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_eba3d5ab		I didn't invade her thoughts intentionally, but her emotions made them pour out like a rushing river, impossible to ignore.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	648	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_76fa7ab1		I saw her as a child, running hand in hand with my mother through the sunlit gardens of Kyeongjang. Their laughter was soft and carefree, playing simple games and playing with toys.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	649	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_46b84367		The memories shifted. I watched them grow older, their bond remaining unshaken. Family gatherings, late-night conversations under the stars, and quiet moments shared in the palace's library.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	650	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_13f99fbb		Another memory surfaced—a dazzling vision of Aunt Ji-hye dressed in the finest silks, the fabric shimmering in the light. It was my mother's wedding day. With my father. Aunt Ji-hye cried. She always does.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	651	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_1eddf7aa		Then the memories darkened, I saw my mother standing before Aunt Ji-hye expressing her desire to venture to Tianho with my father. Aunt cried and begged her to reconsider.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	652	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_5b324a08		The last memory was Aunt knowing of my father and mother's fate. Captain Sunwoo was there, comforting her. We were there too. Me and Jong-hee.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	653	"[what]"
