ch4_chunghee_qtc_d171691b		Her eyes widened as she realized what I intended to do.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	696	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_e5ae90c4	ji_hye	Chung, no! Don't do this. Please, I'm begging you—	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	698	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_f5c4a543		Before she could finish, I closed my eyes, channeling my focus. My mind reached into hers, gently but firmly quieting her frantic thoughts.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	700	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_0641a2fd		A gentle focused thought. And I encouraged her to drift into a peaceful slumber.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	701	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_3dcdccad	ji_hye	Oh… I - Yes. I feel sleepy…	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	703	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_783f2bc6	ji_hye	So… sleepy…	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	704	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_d3d945c6		Aunt Ji-hye blinked a few times. Slowly, she sank to her knees, her eyelids fluttering closed as she succumbed to an unnatural, peaceful slumber.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	706	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_07cdb3e8		I stepped forward, catching her before she could slump to the cold stone floor.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	707	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_4f81180b	ji_hye	Zzz…. Zzz…	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	709	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_c393c70b		Carefully, I carried her to the spare sofa in the corner of the room.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	711	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_5f57ae6f	chung_hee	I'm sorry, Aunt. I promise… I will return.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	713	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_34771a45		As I straightened, I sensed him before I saw him.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	715	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_c3584177	captain_sunwoo	Pyeha, it's Kang Sunwoo. May I enter?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	718	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_d5a8e95e		I turned, composing myself as the door opened. Captain Sunwoo stepped inside, his sharp gaze immediately noticing Ji-Hye's sleeping form. His brow furrowed, but he bowed deeply before me.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	720	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_d809c063	captain_sunwoo	Pyeha, I see that the Royal Advisor is… resting. I hope I am not intruding.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	722	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_c118d7e9	chung_hee	You are not. She was overwhelmed and needed rest. I trust you will keep your voice low, Captain.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	723	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_257234d4		He straightened, his eyes flicking to the glowing amulet in my hand before returning to meet mine.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	725	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_112ba89b	captain_sunwoo	Pyeha, forgive me for my boldness, but I understand you intend to leave the palace tonight. I must implore you to reconsider.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	727	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_11a874cf	chung_hee	Captain, I appreciate your concern, but my decision is final.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	728	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_dd6fca55	captain_sunwoo	Then allow me to accompany you, Pyeha. If you insist on facing danger, I will not let you face it alone.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	729	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_51d8818e	chung_hee	Your place is here, Sunwoo. Kyeongjang needs its captain, and I need you to protect what I leave behind. This is my burden to bear.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	730	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_0c1692a1		The amulet in my hand began to glow brighter, its golden runes spiraling outward as I prepared to activate it.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	732	"[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_7058b32c	captain_sunwoo	Pyeha—	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	734	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_ac8170f1	chung_hee	Take care of Aunt Ji-hye. And Jong-hee… tell him I will return.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	735	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_chunghee_qtc_fe067001		Captain Sunwoo carried Aunt Ji-hye and left the room.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	737	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_81a4d1a6		The heavy wooden door to the storage creaked open. A figure entered. It was Captain Sunwoo.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	752	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_31c7e58a		Upon entering, he bowed deeply, the moonlight glinting off the metal plates of his uniform.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	753	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_b2e64480	captain_sunwoo	Pyeha. Forgive my intrusion, but I have come at Ji-Hye's request. She feared for you.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	755	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_common_1_fb0de5f8		I turned to face him fully.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	757	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_08d59483	chung_hee	Captain Sunwoo. You should know better than to interrupt the Emperor Lord's solitude.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	759	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_common_1_5cc6d262	captain_sunwoo	Pyeha, I… I mean no disrespect. But if I may speak freely…	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	760	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_common_1_c13b882d	captain_sunwoo	Please don't do this… this path you are planning to choose is a perilous one.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	761	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_common_1_a1c85572		I raised an eyebrow.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	763	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_3c6eb64c	chung_hee	You think I do not know that, Captain? You think I haven't considered the risks?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	765	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_common_1_a61c7754		He kept his head bowed earnestly. Aunt Ji-hye held my hand tightly.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	768	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_0a42dd86	ji_hye	Chung… Please… *crying*	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	770	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_common_1_abdf9318	captain_sunwoo	I do not doubt your wisdom, Pyeha. But the burden of vengeance is not yours to bear alone.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	771	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_common_1_84f34646	captain_sunwoo	If it is vengeance you seek, then allow me to gather the most skilled soldiers of Kyeongjang. Let us march together, and I swear by my honor, Pyeha and Pyeha-sshi will be avenged.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	772	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_common_1_0ce12f90	chung_hee	This is something I must do on my own, Captain. Kyeongjang will not suffer more losses on my behalf.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	773	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_common_1_f5dc96ad	captain_sunwoo	Pyeha… please reconsider. Your safety is paramount. If you fall, the empire—	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	774	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_common_1_2e7c893f	chung_hee	The empire will endure. It has endured before. And I will not fall.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	775	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_common_1_59854855		Sunwoo's gaze faltered. He bowed his head low.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	777	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_40980bdf	captain_sunwoo	Then may the Tetrad watch over you, Pyeha.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	779	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_common_1_84520eb2		Both of them looked at each other and looked down.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	781	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_d3974b51	ji_hye	If you are truly set on this path, Chung, then all I can do is wish you safety. Please… come back to us. Come back to Jong-hee.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	783	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_common_1_f98e9332	chung_hee	I will return, Aunt. I swear it.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	784	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_common_1_4f95b7f6		Her trembling hands touched my face, her eyes searching mine one last time before stepping back.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	786	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_4116088a	ji_hye	Then I have nothing left to say except… goodbye, my Emperor Lord. May your journey be swift, and may justice be yours.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	788	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_common_1_e5ff25ad		Captain Sunwoo stood up and approached Aunt Ji-hye.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	790	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_230e2bda	captain_sunwoo	Royal Advisor. Would you care to walk back with me?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	792	captain_sunwoo "[what]"
ch4_common_1_835b8f4e	ji_hye	Yes, Captain Sunwoo. I appreciate your kind offer.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	793	ji_hye "[what]"
ch4_common_1_1f86d92c		As they turned to leave, Aunt Ji-hye paused at the doorway, glancing back over her shoulder. Her lips trembled as though she wanted to speak, but she said nothing.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	795	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_616e621f		Instead, she gave me a small, bittersweet smile before disappearing into the shadows with Captain Sunwoo.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	796	"[what]"
ch4_common_1_491702a1		Love you Jong-hee. Aunt Ji-Hye. Please forgive me.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	798	"[what]"
ch4_common_2_ffe67c8b		I clutched the amulet of teleportation in my hand. Its emerald glow pulsated with raw energy, illuminating the dark corners of the room.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	813	"[what]"
ch4_common_2_229490b1		Sparks of green light danced along its golden edges.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	816	"[what]"
ch4_common_2_81ba719e		I took a deep breath, steadying my resolve. My heartbeat slowed, my focus narrowing to a single thought—the place I needed to be.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	817	"[what]"
ch4_common_2_1baa2e36	chung_hee	Almighty Renji, Keeper of the Void and Sovereign of Time and Space, I beseech your power. Let your authority guide me across this mortal plane.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	821	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_common_2_0563741d	chung_hee	Deliver me to my destination, that I may fulfill what destiny demands.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	822	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_common_2_cb8a80b1		The room seemed to hold its breath. For a moment, everything stilled. Then, the amulet pulsed violently, its glow intensifying. I felt its power surging through me, a searing heat that seemed to burn through my very essence, yet left no mark on my flesh.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	824	"[what]"
ch4_common_2_b280ba25	chung_hee	To Tianho…	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	826	chung_hee "[what]"
ch4_common_2_f0270edd		Then I vanished into the void.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	828	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_72542112		Tianho	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	850	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_2a3a451d		It had been eight months since Elias and I came to Tianho. Yuxuan graciously gave us a small house for us to live in —not far from his grand manor.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	857	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_4880b5a0		Our house was a little far from the main city. The city itself was a shadow of what I remembered. Once bustling and grand, it was now quieter. What was where high buildings once was, were just small makeshift houses and delapidated structures.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	858	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_ca8af0ca		Yuxuan's manor, however, was a different story. The sprawling estate stood like a testament to prosperity, its large halls and manicured gardens untouched by time. A faint scent of jasmine lingered everywhere, as if the very air itself had been perfumed.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	859	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_391f21bb		Despite the grandeur, Yuxuan at some times, didn't sleep there. One of the maids mentioned it in passing, but she didn't elaborate on where he stayed instead, and I didn't pry.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	860	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_0adca74e		He would often invite Elias and me over to his manor for meals, celebrations, or simply to spend the night in one of the many guest rooms.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	861	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_8ed5f6d3		Sometimes, he would find excuses to linger, sharing stories from his travels or discussing matters of the empire that I could tell he wished to unburden himself of.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	862	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_623ea9ad		Other times, he would vanish for days, leaving the manor unusually quiet. It was a routine I'd come to expect, though the unpredictability of it still caught me off guard.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	863	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_e7903342		In those eight months, life moved forward quietly. Elias, my little light in the darkness, would often dress in skirts and adorn himself with flowers to match Tedda. Whatever makes him happy, I suppose.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	864	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_e93bf46c		The amulet that Elias once had stopped glowing entirely. It's like the power inside had been all used up. Good riddance.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	865	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_d4c23bb9		For me, I spent my time rebuilding—physically, mentally, emotionally. I was no longer the Dragon of Gale in the sense that I once was. My days were simpler now, filled with quiet reflection and attempts to find a purpose beyond the shadow of loss.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	868	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_7b8da897		The Dragon of Gale is dead.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	869	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_03c33773		Yuxuan had invited me more than once to visit my family's graves. Each time, I declined. It wasn't that I didn't want to go—it was that I couldn't.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	870	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_23e7e59b		The thought of standing before their final resting place, of facing the reality of their absence, was something I couldn't bring myself to do.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	871	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_efdef22a		Until now.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	872	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_d11297a4		Tomorrow marks the fifth anniversary of the tragedy of Tianho. Five years since that fateful day when everything changed, when the world as I knew it was shattered.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	873	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_4dc84000		I turned to Elias, who had been sitting on the rug, giggling as he carefully tied a chain of flowers around Tedda's neck.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	875	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_532b4b1d	dorian	Elias… I think I'm ready.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	877	dorian "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_108f6ef1	elias	Ready for what, daddy?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	878	elias "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_7b1ca467		Before I could answer, Yuxuan stepped into the room, his robes sweeping softly against the wooden floor. He had been reading in the corner, but now his full attention was on me.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	880	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_fbb4ff15	yuxuan	For what, Dorian?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	882	yuxuan "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_7c9c2e8f	dorian	To visit their graves. maybe now is the time.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	883	dorian "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_ae620cd9		Yuxuan expression softened. He set the book aside and crossed the room, placing a reassuring hand on my shoulder.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	885	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_7a5d9901	yuxuan	Praise the Prosperity Dragon. If you're ready, then I'll go with you.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	887	yuxuan "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_607d7c28		I hesitated, glancing at the darkened sky outside the window. The thought of Empress Olympia lingered in the back of my mind—a ripple of unease that I couldn't shake.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	889	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_34fd6e39	dorian	Do you think we could go now? I'd rather avoid running into the Empress of Gale if we can help it.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	891	dorian "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_465ed9a5		Yuxuan nodded without hesitation.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	893	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_1ee07957	yuxuan	Sure!	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	895	yuxuan "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_c6da801f		Before I could respond, Elias sprang to his feet, clutching Tedda tightly to his chest.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	897	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_2a3f0cbf	elias	Ooh! Can me and Tedda come, daddy?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	899	elias "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_0e93fbfb		Tedda: …	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	900	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_009e3c61		Tedda remained silent, as always, but Elias made sure to shake the little toy, as if demanding my agreement.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	903	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_d411a0ef		I knelt in front of him, placing a gentle hand on his head.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	904	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_21d531c7	dorian	I don't think it's a good idea… This isn't the kind of trip for you.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	906	dorian "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_e0485ba9	yuxuan	Oh, come now, Dorian. Let him come along. There are plenty of food stalls along the way. I'm sure Elias and Tedda would enjoy that, wouldn't you, Elias?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	907	yuxuan "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_4e7705e3	elias	Food? Like dumplings? And candy sticks? Ooooh, Tedda loves candy sticks!	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	908	elias "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_b44b9db4		He spun in a little circle, holding Tedda above his head.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	910	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_74adbadf	dorian	Alright, but you have to promise me you'll stay close. No running off, understand?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	912	dorian "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_265bd757	yuxuan	Alright. It's settled. I'll have the carriage waiting!	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	913	yuxuan "[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_045987e1		The ride to the cemetery was quiet, save for the soft creak of the carriage wheels and the occasional chatter from Elias.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	917	"[what]"
ch4_tianho_dorian_aff8ab42		He sat in Yuxuan's lap, happily pointing out passing trees and the occasional bird. I stayed silent, lost in my thoughts, the weight of what lay ahead pressing down on me.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	918	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_4c8482d0		It took thirty minutes to get there. The cemetery was modest yet serene, nestled on the outskirts of the city. A handful of people wandered among the gravestones, some kneeling in prayer, others buying food at small booths set up nearby.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	935	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_b6ae2f1e	yuxuan	Take your time, Dorian. Elias and I will wander around for a bit.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	937	yuxuan "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_dc40d141	elias	Tedda and I will wait for you, daddy!	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	938	elias "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_737f925d	dorian	Stay close to Yuxuan, alright?	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	939	dorian "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_c61e02ad		And just like that, I was alone.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	944	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_2d8acd96		The morning wind whispered through the trees, carrying with it a faint chill that seeped into my bones. I took a deep breath and began to walk.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	945	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_1ac68f04		Yuxuan had given me directions before we arrived, and I followed the path he described. It felt endless, each step heavier than the last.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	946	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_13b7ae2e		Then I saw them.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	949	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_e6557096		Their graves stood together in a quiet corner of the cemetery, the tombstones slightly weathered by time but still standing firm. The carvings were intricate, their names etched in flowing script that seemed to glisten under the morning light.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	950	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_08dfc203		Elara Burnham. Daniel. Emily. Sarah. Lucas.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	951	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_b3b9e7f1		My family.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	952	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_97c0dc2d		My breath caught in my throat as I stared at the names, each one a sharp reminder of what I had lost. My knees felt weak, and before I knew it, I had fallen to the ground in front of them.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	954	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_e4a86698		I reached out, my fingers brushing against Elara's name. The cold stone beneath my hand was a stark contrast to the warmth she had always carried.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	955	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_8f394f96	dorian	My love, my heart...	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	963	dorian "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_c27ebc99		The words came out in a whisper, trembling with emotion.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	965	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_90cc2ec9	dorian	It's been years. I've missed you all so much.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	967	dorian "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_16c7097e		I swallowed hard, my vision blurring as tears welled up in my eyes.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	969	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_1093e2f4	dorian	I've been wandering for so long, trying to find my place in this world. But I never forgot you, and I never will.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	971	dorian "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_6483ae93		My voice cracked as I choked back a sob.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	973	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_5e28bab3	dorian	I'm so sorry for everything. I should have protected you. I should have been there with you all.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	975	dorian "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_49bcc34e		I stayed there, sitting in silence as the wind carried the soft rustle of leaves. My mind drifted back to memories of them—Elara's laugh, Daniel's courage, Emily's curiosity, Sarah's wisdom, and little Lucas's boundless energy.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	977	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_1199372d		Time seemed to slip away as I sat there, lost in thought. I didn't know how long it had been when I finally looked up, noticing more people arriving at the cemetery. The peaceful solitude was beginning to fade, and I realized it was time to leave.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	978	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_0633f826		I stood, brushing off the dirt from my knees, and looked down at the tombstones one last time.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	979	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_e17bc1d9	dorian	I wish I could stay longer, but I need to get a move on.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	981	dorian "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_f05dde64		The words felt hollow as they left my lips.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	983	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_8efe3681		I lingered for a moment longer, my fingers grazing Elara's name once more.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	984	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_8560098f	dorian	See you in my dreams, I guess.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	986	dorian "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_134be9ca		I turned and began walking back toward the entrance.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	988	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_73e0c737		I couldn't find Yuxuan at his previous location. I scanned the area. Then I found Elias.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	994	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_9e747bee		He was perched atop a gravestone, his little legs swinging back and forth as he cuddled Tedda close. A bouquet of wildflowers rested beside him.	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	997	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_f144727e	elias	Tedda, look at the pretty flowers. They're so colorful!	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	999	elias "[what]"
ch4_cemetery_0e93fbfb		Tedda: …	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	1000	"[what]"
ch4_cemetery_883305ca	elias	This one's my favorite, Tedda. It's the same color as your nose!	game/06_chapter_04.rpy	1001	elias "[what]"
