ch5_niko_common_9ddf5c6a		I exhaled sharply, shaking my head, trying to push past the echoes clawing at my mind. My fists clenched.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	676	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_7931b3e3		I looked at him, my voice tight.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	677	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_9562179d	dorian	Why? Why do you worship such a deity?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	679	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_d83f39b2	dorian	Surely you were there that night. The night of the tragedy. You saw what happened.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	680	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_3d9be40b		A beat of silence. Then another.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	682	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_0514674a		The flames still danced behind my eyes, the screams still clawed at my ears.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	683	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_6e4cbea8	dorian	Those people… They died because of your god.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	685	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_eb5e3cdb		Niko didn't speak right away. Instead, he stepped forward and placed a firm hand on my shoulder.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	687	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_778b9752	niko	You might wanna sit down for this, Dorian.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	689	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_3fe211e5		I resisted at first. My blood still burned, my hands still trembled with the weight of old memories.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	691	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_949b6411		Reluctantly, I sank onto the chair.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	692	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_b7c82b20		He reached into a small folded pouch at his side and pulled out a worn pamphlet.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	693	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_746ca41a	dorian	These are… lovingly made. Did you make these?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	695	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_b2e2a195	niko	No. These were drawn by the orphans we took in.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	696	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_9b7e598b	niko	Children who lost everything—their homes, their families, their past. Me, Kaito and a few other Prophets gave them shelter, a place to start again.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	697	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_7d5cbec5	niko	Me and my fellow brothers in Enoch keep one of these just in case we have the opportunity to share our faith.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	698	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_7dfbe64b		There's a certain purity and warmth in Niko's beliefs that is undeniably endearing. If only his faith were centered around a different deity, like the Tetrad for example, and not the one associated with the events in Tianho, I would have wholeheartedly embraced and admired his devotion.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	700	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_3f4f06e8	dorian	There are lots of drawings here. What's this have to do with the death god?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	702	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_2f139a51	niko	Well, as we all know, the death god is not a static entity but is reincarnated again and again, much like the cycle of life and death it oversees.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	703	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_f1174848		I ran a thumb over the painted pages, my chest still tight.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	705	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_a6a57f69	dorian	So, you worship all of the reincarnations of the death gods. Not just Enoch?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	707	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_e8ff3edc	niko	Precisely. We worship the death god as an entity. However, the most prominent reincarnation of the death god is Enoch of Mjoll.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	708	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_74213b00	niko	Many historians agree that Enoch was the cause of the many changes in Ena: the downfall of the civilization of Kyeongjang, the fall of the tyrant king in Mjoll, the disappearance of the Tetrad gods and the immortal dragons, the abolishment of slavery in the Centennial Isles, and the list goes on.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	709	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_e2293920	niko	He shows the capacity of mankind. He may be a god, but he is also human. Both capable of doing good, and bad. Light and dark. Life and death.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	710	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_f1ff01ca	dorian	I appreciate your explanation about Enoch, but what does this have to do with the death god not being related to the incident in Tianho?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	711	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_bee89a77	niko	In Enoch's final moments, as he lay on his dying bed, he made a solemn vow to his best friend. He swore that in his next lives, he would do everything within his power to right the wrongs he had committed while he was alive.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	712	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_adeeb321	niko	In response to Enoch's oath, his best friend swore a solemn promise of his own. He pledged to seek out the future incarnations of the death gods and guide them toward a path of greater benevolence and good.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	713	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_3cbd10b8	niko	And thus, from those ancient promises, the Prophets of the Death God were founded. A dedicated group of individuals who have taken it upon themselves to seek out and guide the incarnations of the death god, nurturing their potential for benevolence and compassion.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	714	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_6fc29895	niko	I am proud to be one of those people. This is my calling.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	715	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_ad9c858d	dorian	Interesting. How many death gods were influenced by the prophets?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	716	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_108995ae	niko	The first sighting we had was five years ago on Tianho. Our brothers tried to help him, but alas, he was already killed.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	717	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_5c9c32a6		Five years ago?!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	719	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_679c02a2	dorian	Five years ago? That's... surprising. I thought you said that the Prophets were founded four centuries ago. I would have expected the prophets to have encountered and influenced multiple death gods by now.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	721	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_d0919e86	niko	We were. The Prophets have transitioned into a charity organization after the first century it was established. Many of us have already believed that death god's work is complete.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	722	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_407ae018	niko	So, you can imagine the excitement all of us prophets have when the sighting has been made five years ago.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	723	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_2cbe7b65		I could imagine it, all right.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	725	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_83db7500		Four hundred years of waiting, of fading purpose—then suddenly, proof. A reason to move.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	726	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_a8f5716e	dorian	And now you're investigating that sighting. Because you don't believe the creature that destroyed Tianho was the Death God.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	728	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_4c18d23f	niko	Exactly.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	729	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_146dbfba	dorian	Have you gotten any leads?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	730	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_71f319b2		Niko shook his head, frustration evident in the way his fingers curled slightly.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	732	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_c219b873	niko	None. We've searched outside of Tianho. We scoured Gale, Hinami, the borderlands. But there's nothing. No traces. No patterns.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	734	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_2d499b77	niko	Something isn't right, Dorian. We're missing something. We just don't know what.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	735	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_809b83df		Before I could respond, a familiar whirring sound filled the room.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	737	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_10b398dc		The little machine rolled in with a tray, a neat pitcher of warm water and a stack of cups balanced with near-perfect precision. Its screen flickered, displaying an animated image of water being poured.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	741	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_86621f39	roboto	Beep-boop! R-r-r-Roboto has arrived with water delivery!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	743	roboto "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_79fd7442	niko	Roboto, lower your voice.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	744	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_600e8c62		The robot's screen immediately switched to a large 'shhh' icon, accompanied by the sound of static mimicking a whisper.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	746	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_1b935286	roboto	Activating silent mode… Shhhh….	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	748	roboto "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_c7870752		It turned back to us, its voice now hushed.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	750	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_01358843	roboto	H-H-Here is your water, sir. Warm, just as you've requested.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	752	roboto "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_7dfe5d69	niko	Thank you. Just place it beside me, please.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	753	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_c3f9019c		It wobbled forward, carefully placing the tray on the small bedside table. The screen changed again, now showing a satisfied-looking pitcher giving a thumbs-up.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	755	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_ab829005	roboto	Mission accomplished! Would you like Roboto to stay and provide additional hydration support?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	757	roboto "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_8b78406a	dorian	Hydration support?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	758	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_c416c4df	roboto	Roboto can monitor water levels! Fluff pillows! Tuck in patients! Or… or… tell a bedtime story!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	759	roboto "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_cfd35ec9	dorian	Stories, huh? Interesting.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	760	dorian "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_f6d1bf53		Niko yawned, stretching his arms.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	762	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_2955d578	niko	You can stay if you want. Nothing else to do but keep watch.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	764	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_b20bf3b7		Roboto's screen changed again, now displaying a small clock icon.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	766	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_70b3fb0b	roboto	Oh! Speaking of time—it's almost dinner! Master Yuxuan is currently looking for you in the living room, Sir Dorian.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	768	roboto "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_e81dae25		I glanced at Niko, who was already sinking back into his chair, stretching his legs out with a quiet sigh.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	770	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_8ff34c03	niko	Go ahead. I'll keep watch here.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	772	niko "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_94c8f393		I gave him a nod before stepping out, leaving Roboto standing beside the bed, its screen flickering between a neutral expression and a 'standby mode' prompt.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	774	"[what]"
ch5_niko_common_2f52546d	roboto	Please g-g-g-g-go ahead and take a nap, sir Niko. If the patient exhibits irregular breathing patterns, Roboto shall alert you immediately!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	776	roboto "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_98c9f7c9	roboto	Would you like me to turn off the lights?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	777	roboto "[what]"
ch5_niko_common_1fde6ddf	niko	Sure. Thanks.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	778	niko "[what]"
ch5_living_room_d6d9c55c		As I stepped into the main area, the sound of playful giggles filled the air. Laughter bouncing off the walls like sunlight filtering through an open window.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	792	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_ad1f5ed6		Elias was running in circles, his little legs pumping as fast as they could carry him. Close behind, a small boy with messy green hair and oversized glasses was in hot pursuit.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	793	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_abc8c11a	tim	You know I'm gonna catch you, Elias!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	795	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_670de459		Elias let out an exaggerated gasp, clutching his stuffed bear, Tedda, against his chest.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	797	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_e522f91a	elias	Ahh! Haha! Hurry, Tedda! Tim might catch us!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	799	elias "[what]"
ch5_living_room_0e93fbfb		Tedda: …	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	800	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_26b9db05		The kid pushed his glasses up the bridge of his nose.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	802	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_d4f29702	tim	Hmm… If I analyze the velocity of his movements and factor in his diminishing stamina…	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	804	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_bda1aced	tim	A-ha! I have predicted your trajectory!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	805	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_bc2e7144		With sudden speed, Tim lunged, tapping Elias on the shoulder.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	807	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_b18f909d	elias	Hahaha! Aaaaahhh! He got me!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	809	elias "[what]"
ch5_living_room_65f422e3	tim	Mathematical precision. You stood no chance.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	810	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_ad827100		Elias tilted his head.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	812	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_2719fcf3	elias	I dunno what that means, but that was fun!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	814	elias "[what]"
ch5_living_room_847fb70a	tim	Let's have a rematch! I shall implement new strategies to maintain my superior—	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	815	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_4b467189	weng	Tim? Tim! By the stars, Tim… I'm calling you.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	817	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_935535c9		An elderly woman in a crisp white uniform strode toward them, her silver-streaked hair pulled into a neat bun.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	819	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_c07e298e		The little boy let out a small grunt, clearly reluctant to stop playing. He turned his head slightly, brows furrowed.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	820	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_2121f19e	tim	But we're busy, Miss Weng…	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	822	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_7c417e91	weng	Tim, be careful. You might break something again! I don't want a repeat of your Roboto incident.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	823	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_6580770c		His shoulders slumped in defeat.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	825	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_74d7db67	tim	Yes, Miss Weng… Ugh…	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	827	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_7b0f22a8		I glanced at Elias, who was still bouncing on his feet, too absorbed in the game to notice me watching. A small smile tugged at my lips.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	829	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_be703031		It was rare—seeing him like this. Seeing him play with someone other than Tedda. Someone real. Someone his age.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	830	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_08577337		I softened my voice.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	832	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_32c0b118	dorian	Elias, are you having fun?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	834	dorian "[what]"
ch5_living_room_1e7115bd		No response. He was too caught up in his play, bouncing excitedly on his feet.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	836	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_1ed537ca	elias	Tim, should we continue playing tag?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	838	elias "[what]"
ch5_living_room_91638757	tim	Sorry, Elias. But Miss Weng doesn't want me to play tag anymore.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	839	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_9a8816ce	elias	Aww… But… But—	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	840	elias "[what]"
ch5_living_room_b861cb95	tim	That's okay! We can still tell stories!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	841	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_88f198a1	elias	Oh… Okay!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	842	elias "[what]"
ch5_living_room_7b550510	tim	I'll start! There's a huge library here! And my favorite story is the one about the kumiho and—	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	843	tim "[what]"
ch5_living_room_8b74c6a9		Yuxuan approached me, his usual easygoing smirk in place. He gestured toward the green-haired kid.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	845	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_7e4663aa	yuxuan	So that's Tim. The one playing with Elias.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	847	yuxuan "[what]"
ch5_living_room_111f7e19	dorian	He and Elias are getting along well. I'm happy.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	848	dorian "[what]"
ch5_living_room_27da4667	yuxuan	It's good for him. Kids need company.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	849	yuxuan "[what]"
ch5_living_room_3ee6b359		He then turned to the elderly woman, motioning toward me.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	851	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_4f4d4f4c	yuxuan	Soooo, this is Cai Weng. Miss Weng, this is Dorian Burnham.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	853	yuxuan "[what]"
ch5_living_room_ff7933b7	yuxuan	Weng is a true gem. She's my personal assistant, my cook, my all-rounder here at this laboratory.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	854	yuxuan "[what]"
ch5_living_room_34645bf2	weng	Oh, you're too kind, Master Yuxuan. I'm just doing my job. It's a pleasure to be of service here. Is that right, Tim?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	855	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_e991c08d		Tim was still too focused on Elias. Elias giggles and waves Tedda around.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	857	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_451f0edf	weng	…*sighs* Kids…	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	859	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_e90ac704		She turned to me with a polite nod.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	861	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_ff0f34d2	weng	Pleasure to meet you, Sir Burnham.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	863	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_25ff1dac	dorian	Likewise, Miss Weng.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	864	dorian "[what]"
ch5_living_room_8d90bcd4		I chuckled under my breath, watching Elias laugh as he exchanged stories with Tim.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	866	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_48a038fe		Yuxuan told me that Svante, the aldorith who realized who I was, was placed in the storage room.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	867	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_9fa7cdcc		Isn't that dangerous? Svante's a metal channeler, as we've seen a while ago. He might turn on us.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	868	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_66510728		Miss Weng tells me that Svante's been handcuffed with Jinyan steel which suppresses channeling.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	869	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_3623e242	yuxuan	By the way, Svante—the Aldorith who figured out who you were? I had him placed in the storage room.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	871	yuxuan "[what]"
ch5_living_room_e07d4c00		I turned to him sharply.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	873	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_fd7d3a3f	dorian	Isn't that dangerous? He's a metal channeler. We saw what he could do earlier. He might turn on us.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	875	dorian "[what]"
ch5_living_room_cdea4233		Before Yuxuan could answer, Weng let out a small chuckle, shaking her head.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	877	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_85b8681b	weng	No need to worry, Sir Burnham. The aldorith's been properly restrained.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	879	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_27841356		She gestured toward her wrist, mimicking the snap of cuffs.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	881	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_10f84e58	weng	We restrained him with Jinyan Steel—he shouldn't be a problem now.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	883	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_cf1046f9		That caught my attention. Jinyan Steel—extremely rare, ridiculously expensive. I'd only used it once before, back when I had to subdue a particularly powerful channeler. The material didn't just restrain—it completely suppressed channeling.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	885	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_8b35b458		I'm not surprised Yuxuan has some here, given his wealth and influence.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	886	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_e3f49920	dorian	And he's just… sitting in there?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	888	dorian "[what]"
ch5_living_room_589bf021	yuxuan	Fast asleep. Thanks to the Cheng Industries' Sleeping Powder.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	889	yuxuan "[what]"
ch5_living_room_963bbad6		Weng's gaze flickered toward the clock hanging on the wall.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	891	"[what]"
ch5_living_room_3742a6f0	weng	Speaking of sleep, it's already past dinner time… No wonder I'm feeling lightheaded.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	893	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_4908db3d	weng	I need to hurry. You must be hungry, Master Yuxuan. Sir Burnham.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	894	weng "[what]"
ch5_living_room_21b03e11	dorian	Just a little.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	895	dorian "[what]"
