ch5_dinner_talk_bf771320	svante	Huh? Chanmong…	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2615	svante "[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_aae75f84	chung_hee	Cheonmyeong Gyeol… A duel between two rulers to the death.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2616	chung_hee "[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_3b66e5ea		The words seemed to echo through our minds.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2618	"[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_c034be83		For a moment, nobody spoke. Then, from the far end of the table—	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2619	"[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_23df9f32		Tim straightened, his eyes widening with recognition.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2620	"[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_85af7c7e	tim	Wait… you mean the ancient trials of Kyeongjang? The ones that determined a kingdom's fate with a single battle?	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2622	tim "[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_f0602bae	tim	I've read that before! In pre-Enoch books!	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2623	tim "[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_bc3d4423		Chung-hee gave a single nod.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2625	"[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_d5d8d3a6	chung_hee	Yes. It is an ancient tradition, one older than any war on record.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2627	chung_hee "[what]"
ch5_dinner_talk_aa1921d0	chung_hee	Long ago, the rulers of old would stake their lives in battle rather than sacrifice their people to war. A single duel—no armies, no bloodshed beyond their own. The winner would decide the fate of nations. It was a trial of honor, strength, and destiny.	game/07_chapter_05.rpy	2628	chung_hee "[what]"
