ch9_common_3d444cc5	dorian	...What is all of this for, Miss Weng?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	360	dorian "[what]"
ch9_common_2d3bd393	weng	Today is the Fifth Anniversary of the Tragedy of Tianho, sir Dorian. Aside from our group, I'll be cooking for the employees and their families as well.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	361	weng "[what]"
ch9_common_82928abb	weng	Far be it from Master Yuxuan to let his staff, Gao, Jiang, and their families, observe the day without delicious food on the table.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	362	weng "[what]"
ch9_common_c9370f7a		The words struck me like a fist to the chest. My breath hitched. That's right.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	364	"[what]"
ch9_common_e0076399		How could I have forgotten?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	365	"[what]"
ch9_common_78c8791f		Weng wiped her hands on a towel, her voice calm yet thoughtful.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	367	"[what]"
ch9_common_9c4bf2d6	weng	Master Yuxuan left earlier to meet with the representatives from the Hinami Kingdom. Hinami will be hosting today's program.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	369	weng "[what]"
ch9_common_f10c5079		That made sense. Hinami was always the first to extend a hand in times of remembrance.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	371	"[what]"
ch9_common_34f9a62b	dorian	I'm not surprised. Their customs place great value on honoring the dead-especially their burial rites.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	373	dorian "[what]"
ch9_common_30421a3f		Svante leaned forward slightly, holding a tomato, curiosity flickering in his violet eyes.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	375	"[what]"
ch9_common_ed26e77d	svante	What kind of customs, sir? Sorry, I'm not too familiar with Hinami's traditions. Father forbade us from stepping outside of Mjoll.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	377	svante "[what]"
ch9_common_0a207a88	magnus	I must admit, I too am unfamiliar. Can you enlighten us, Dorian?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	378	magnus "[what]"
ch9_common_99c6e0f2	dorian	For starters, they sink their dead to the bottom of the ocean. To them, the ocean isn't just a body of water-it's an eternal resting place, where souls drift into the embrace of the Dragon of the Depths.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	379	dorian "[what]"
ch9_common_7fb59572	svante	...Wait. They just-sink them?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	380	svante "[what]"
ch9_common_01c44d49	weng	Indeed. I've read many accounts of their reverence for the Dragon of the Depths.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	381	weng "[what]"
ch9_common_304ba312	weng	They believe the sea carries their ancestors' spirits, guiding them to where they belong. It's a deeply sacred ritual.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	382	weng "[what]"
ch9_common_d6feb614		Magnus paused, turning to face me with a contemplative frown.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	384	"[what]"
ch9_common_bebd8ab8	magnus	But if the dead are scattered across the ocean, how do the living visit their loved ones? Graves, shrines-these are markers, places of remembrance.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	386	magnus "[what]"
ch9_common_91c2e06a	magnus	How does one pay respects when the resting place is... endless?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	387	magnus "[what]"
ch9_common_8edbc10c	weng	That's a good point. Do they have any traditions to compensate for that?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	388	weng "[what]"
ch9_common_e397226f	dorian	Honestly? I don't know.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	389	dorian "[what]"
ch9_common_b5473af5	roboto	The e-e-e-entire ocean. Whenever they s-s-s-see the ocean, they remember them. Their memory is not confined to a single place.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	390	roboto "[what]"
ch9_common_c9a82c85	svante	Really? That's amazing.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	391	svante "[what]"
ch9_common_72e51cf9	tedda_alive	Leave it to Mister Roboto to give a quick answer!!	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	393	tedda_alive "[what]"
ch9_common_aa39674a		Roboto blinked, its glowing eyes whirring slightly.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	395	"[what]"
ch9_common_f0b127d3	roboto	Y-Y-Y-You can always count on Robotooooo, sir Svanteee~~	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	397	roboto "[what]"
ch9_common_27900ccc		Magnus, intrigued, tapped a finger against his chin.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	399	"[what]"
ch9_common_66daf093	magnus	A profound perspective. To be remembered not by stone, but by the endless tides. Hm...	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	401	magnus "[what]"
ch9_common_228df9f2	svante	Have you ever been to Hinami, sir Dorian?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	402	svante "[what]"
ch9_common_bbb7e3c6		I shook my head.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	404	"[what]"
