ch9_common_4445a45b		I exhaled, running a hand through my hair. Whatever I liked, huh?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	456	"[what]"
ch9_library_a7582dde		I decided to visit Yuxuan's library, hoping to clear my head. The weight of the day pressed against my shoulders, and I needed a moment to breathe, to escape into something else-anything else.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	499	"[what]"
ch9_library_b4f9e1cc		I had never actually been to his library before. I had heard about it in passing, mentioned in Yuxuan's half-hearted grumbles about keeping track of rare texts, and Tim and Elias going there on my first day inside Yuxuan's underground library.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	500	"[what]"
ch9_library_106b8a49		As I walked down the stone hallway, my thoughts drifted. When was the last time I even read a book?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	501	"[what]"
ch9_library_8b499d60		I remembered my time as a Paladin in the service of Empress Olympia. We had a special library, a grand hall dedicated solely to the knowledge that Paladins were meant to wield. Not just books on war strategy and elemental channeling, but history, philosophy, even works of art.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	502	"[what]"
ch9_library_f76efb83		I recalled the way we used to tease Feng for his love of romance novels. He never hid it-on the contrary, he would often sit with a book in one hand and his sword in the other, completely engrossed in some dramatic tale of love and tragedy.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	503	"[what]"
ch9_library_47e5a05a		I smirked to myself. Far be it from me to read romantic novels. Or maybe...	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	504	"[what]"
ch9_library_43b153ee		Maybe I could read some poetry. There was a poet from Hinami whose works I had once admired.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	505	"[what]"
ch9_library_91d45ed5		I reached the door and pushed it open. A gust of cool air met me, carrying the scent of aged parchment, ink, and ancient wood.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	506	"[what]"
ch9_library_2b8296fa		It was unlike anything I had ever seen.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	507	"[what]"
ch9_library_e485e923		Mahogany bookshelves stretched as far as the eye could see, their golden inlays shimmering under the glow of soft, floating lanterns. The ceiling loomed far above me, at least forty feet high, with delicate metal bridges connecting the upper floors.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	508	"[what]"
ch9_library_ac08dbaa		Everywhere I turned, books, books, books-stories waiting to be unraveled, secrets of the past preserved in brittle pages.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	509	"[what]"
ch9_library_b1bd1e92		At the far end of the library, a massive hourglass stood on a pedestal, its grains of sand moving slowly, almost as if time itself was sluggish within this place.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	510	"[what]"
ch9_library_b321167f		Seated at one of the long tables in the center, surrounded by open books and scattered notes, was Chung-hee.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	511	"[what]"
ch9_library_7f383f38		Chung-hee didn't even glance up when I approached. His eyes remained fixed on the pages before him, scanning each line with sharp, unwavering focus. His brow furrowed slightly, his lips pressed together in concentration.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	512	"[what]"
ch9_library_937cecdc		The only indication that he even registered my presence was a small flick of his fingers, wordlessly gesturing for me to sit-as if I were just another book settling into place in the grand archive.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	513	"[what]"
ch9_library_1cbce6ee		I took a seat across from him, watching as he turned a page with the kind of delicate precision one would use when handling something ancient and fragile.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	514	"[what]"
ch9_library_c4283710		The silence stretched. I cleared my throat.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	515	"[what]"
ch9_library_1f9a1f87	dorian	Hey, Chung. What are you reading?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	517	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_9850f53c		Nothing.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	519	"[what]"
ch9_library_8a44b18e		I tilted my head, glancing at the book in front of him. I couldn't make out all of the text, but I recognized diagrams of ancient seals, detailed notes about ice and-was that a passage about divine imprisonment?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	520	"[what]"
ch9_library_888cf838		He turned another page, his expression unreadable.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	521	"[what]"
ch9_library_d2f290c0	dorian	Chung?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	523	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_02e500c1	chung_hee	Hm? Sorry...	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	524	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_c269299d		A pause. His fingers hovered over the text, hesitating just for a second, as if debating whether my question warranted an answer. Then, with an air of finality, he set his hand down.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	526	"[what]"
ch9_library_d8864525	chung_hee	I'm reading about Magnus. The Divine Weapon.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	528	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_8d83ef10	dorian	Divine Weapon? You think Magnus is the Divine Weapon King Gustav was after?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	529	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_5d8a7842		Before I could press him further, he flipped back a few pages, cross-referencing something in the text. His fingers began tapping against the wooden table, a nervous habit I had come to recognize-his mind was racing, processing faster than he could communicate.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	531	"[what]"
ch9_library_8e9b5d16		Then, his thoughts came through, the words sharper, more fragmented than usual.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	532	"[what]"
ch9_library_12d6d6ed	chung_hee	Yes... and no.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	534	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_b2e175a6		I could feel the strain in the voice inside my head. His composure, usually steady and unwavering, cracked ever so slightly.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	536	"[what]"
ch9_library_dd3b8657	chung_hee	Look, I remain unconvinced that the Divine Weapon is merely a fully-grown man with wings.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	538	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_4c650bb1		His thoughts pressed into mine with force.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	540	"[what]"
ch9_library_39be6401	chung_hee	On top of that, I searched his mind thoroughly, there was NOTHING about his memories connected with being a Divine Weapon. None!	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	542	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_f477701a	dorian	You did say that most of his memories weren't there. Does that mean... he lost them? Like amnesia or something?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	543	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_b3bd238d	chung_hee	I'm afraid it is far stranger than that.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	544	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_4785fc50	chung_hee	He did not lose memories, Dorian. Nothing is forgotten by him. It's just as if nothing was there in the first place.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	545	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_ab888fcb	chung_hee	Only select memories were there. I-	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	546	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_354c1935		His grip on the book tightened.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	548	"[what]"
ch9_library_46db9a09	chung_hee	I must uncover the truth. If my lead was mistaken, then what have I been chasing? Have I erred? What would my aunt think? I-	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	550	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_9d461e41		I blinked.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	552	"[what]"
ch9_library_4ebe6e97	dorian	Your aunt?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	554	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_000ebbc1		The moment the words left my mouth, his entire presence changed.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	556	"[what]"
ch9_library_f6e2a077	dorian	Yesterday, the false Yuxuan mentioned that you had an aunt in Kyeongjang. Was that true?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	558	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_6133a99b		The rhythmic tapping of his fingers against the wood ceased. His eyes, which had been darting between pages, now remained fixed, unreadable.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	560	"[what]"
ch9_library_9b392782	chung_hee	It is of no consequence. Forget it.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	562	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_c6735e57		I studied him.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	564	"[what]"
ch9_library_120c4d36	dorian	Chung-	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	566	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_7e519919	chung_hee	Please drop the subject. I must concentrate.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	567	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_cacb3cb5		And just like that, he retreated into his book. Focused.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	569	"[what]"
ch9_library_b7498d8b		I didn't want to let it go. Not this time.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	577	"[what]"
ch9_library_402f21c9		Maybe it was the way he shut down the moment I mentioned his aunt. The way his unshakable presence wavered, if only for a breath.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	578	"[what]"
ch9_library_61e2812e	dorian	Chung, I need to know. Who is your aunt?	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	580	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_c95f6344	dorian	Tell me more, do you have any other family in-	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	581	dorian "[what]"
ch9_library_a51679e6		But before I could even finish, he closed his book with a deliberate, measured thud.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	583	"[what]"
ch9_library_b1ab0143		He turned to face me, his eyes gleaming like polished metal, sharp and unreadable. The weight of his presence settled over me like an invisible force.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	584	"[what]"
ch9_library_d7061f83		Then, in my mind, his voice cut through with the precision of a blade.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	585	"[what]"
ch9_library_15bb1c0e	chung_hee	Dorian. You saved my life. For that, I will always be thankful.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	587	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_d40684b6	chung_hee	But you must understand something. You and I met only yesterday.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	588	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_43929cc6	chung_hee	I hope you don't mistake shared battlefields for shared burdens.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	589	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_d32e82ae		The pressure lifted as quickly as it came, but the silence it left in its wake was suffocating. He was right. I had known him for only a day and a half.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	591	"[what]"
ch9_library_7d50507e		Chung-hee adjusted his sleeve, returning his gaze to his book.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	592	"[what]"
ch9_library_ae8bb539	chung_hee	You will always have my gratitude, but you must learn your place.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	594	chung_hee "[what]"
ch9_library_53fa5e06		I didn't press further.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	599	"[what]"
ch9_library_cf2ec461		If he wasn't ready to talk, then pushing him wouldn't change that. I knew what it was like to have parts of your past locked away, too painful or complicated to bring to light.	game/11_chapter_09_p1.rpy	600	"[what]"
