ch9_lantern_kids_5dd17973		I walked away from the others, lantern in hand, toward a more remote edge of the hill where the moonlight draped the grass like silver thread. I wanted the moment to be quiet. Private. The wind was gentle here, and the stars looked like they were listening.	game/12_chapter_09_p2.rpy	1876	"[what]"
ch9_lantern_kids_ff85260c		I knelt down beside a smooth stone and studied the blank canvas of the lantern.	game/12_chapter_09_p2.rpy	1877	"[what]"
ch9_lantern_kids_f3c54df8		Elara. Daniel. Emily. Sarah. Lucas.	game/12_chapter_09_p2.rpy	1878	"[what]"
ch9_lantern_kids_9cbb48d5		It was only yesterday that I stood at their graves again, after five long years. It still didn't feel real. As if time had stretched and folded itself in strange ways, and grief had learned to hide in the folds.	game/12_chapter_09_p2.rpy	1879	"[what]"
ch9_lantern_kids_b7f3abcd		I paused.	game/12_chapter_09_p2.rpy	1880	"[what]"
